      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office has operated in Coal City continuously since 1877, anchoring the community for over a century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coal_City%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The arrival of the Cincinnati & Terre Haute Railway through Coal City in 1879 sparked a boom that made the town thrive.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coal_City%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Coal City was officially platted in 1875, just a couple of miles west of the former town of Stockton.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coal_City%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "When the Stockton post office closed in 1879, businesses shifted to Coal City, cementing its status as the local hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
